+1. Microsoft SEAL 4.1.2
+-----------------------
+
+Source: https://github.com/microsoft/SEAL (version 4.1.2), MIT License.
+
+Ported from SEAL (derived code):
+
+- crates/ckks-train-ckks/src/encoder.rs: the bit-reversed negacyclic DWT
+  (util::DWTHandler::transform_to_rev / transform_from_rev), the complex root table
+  (util::ComplexRoots) and the CKKSEncoder slot index map (matrix_reps_index_map_), ported
+  so that encodings agree with SEAL coefficient by coefficient.
+
+Written against the SEAL 4.1.2 sources to reproduce its results or formats (interop):
+
+- crates/ckks-train-ckks/src/params.rs: the prime assignment order of CoeffModulus::Create.
+- crates/ckks-train-core/src/baseconv.rs: the formulas of BaseConverter::fast_convert_array and
+  of divide_and_round_q_last (rescale / mod_down) for one special prime.
+- crates/ckks-train-core/src/ntt.rs: the NTT root and storage conventions.
+- crates/ckks-train-ckks/src/seal_compat.rs: the SEAL serialization format (SEALHeader,
+  Ciphertext / Plaintext / key layouts) and parms_id. The BLAKE2b used for parms_id is an
+  independent implementation from RFC 7693, not SEAL code.
+- crates/ckks-train-ckks/src/encoder.rs (tests): known-answer values printed by SEAL.
+
+Not distributed with hekit: the tools under tools/seal-kat/ and the spikes under spikes/
+build against SEAL fetched by CMake FetchContent; no SEAL source file is vendored in this
+repository.
